      {
        "id": "p10-q2-j",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{1}{x+1}=\\frac{5x-6}{6x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac35$ or $x=2$",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne-1,0$, multiply by $6x(x+1)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}6x&=(5x-6)(x+1)\\\\6x&=5x^2-x-6\\\\5x^2-7x-6&=0\\\\5x^2-10x+3x-6&=0\\\\5x(x-2)+3(x-2)&=0\\\\(5x+3)(x-2)&=0\\\\5x+3&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x-2=0\\\\x&=-\\frac35\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=2\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values satisfy the original equation.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
