      {
        "id": "p10-q2-l",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "l",
        "prompt": "$x+\\frac1x=\\frac{13}{6}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac23$ or $x=\\frac32$",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne0$, multiply by $6x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}6x^2+6&=13x\\\\6x^2-13x+6&=0\\\\6x^2-9x-4x+6&=0\\\\3x(2x-3)-2(2x-3)&=0\\\\(3x-2)(2x-3)&=0\\\\3x-2&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad 2x-3=0\\\\x&=\\frac23\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=\\frac32\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values satisfy the original equation.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 72
