      {
        "id": "p10-q2-m",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "m",
        "prompt": "$\\frac3{x-1}=\\frac{3x-2}{x(x-2)}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-2$",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne0,1,2$, multiply by $x(x-1)(x-2)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3x(x-2)&=(3x-2)(x-1)\\\\3x^2-6x&=3x^2-5x+2\\\\-6x&=-5x+2\\\\-x&=2\\\\x&=-2\\end{align*}$$\nThis value satisfies the original equation.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
